      "problem": "Calculate the discriminant of the quadratic equation $4(x-2)^{2}-8=0.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, note that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(x-2)^{2}-8 & =4({x}^{2}-4x+4)-8 \\\\  & =4{x}^{2}-16x+16-8 \\\\  & =4{x}^{2}-16x+8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe have $a=4,$ $b=-16,$ and $c=8.$ So, we calculate the discriminant as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & ={b}^{2}-4ac \\\\  & =(-16)^{2}-4(4)(8) \\\\  & =256-128 \\\\  & =128\\end{aligned}\n$$",
